|##
##|(markdown) text_1
# Querying JSON Data

DuckDB can read JSON files directly, and Malloy makes it simple to transform the resulting data. The example below reads exchange rate data from the US Treasury and shows the data by currency over time.
|##

source: exchange_rates is 
  duckdb.table('exchange_rates.json')

##|(markdown) text_2
## Query by Country
This query builds a line chart showing exchange rate values over time. With a simple Malloy query, we can easily transform and analyze a dataset directly from an HTTP API, without any intermediate database required.
|##

source: exchange_rates_tiles is exchange_rates extend {
  #(docs) limit=5000 size=large
  view: tile_1 is {
    group_by: data.country_currency_desc
    # line_chart
    nest: by_date is  {
      group_by: data.record_date
      aggregate: rate is data.avg(data.exchange_rate::number)
    }
  }
}
